## Error Handling

### Standard Error Format

All errors follow this format:

```json
{
  "error": "ERROR_CODE",
  "message": "Human-readable message",
  "status": 400,
  "details": {
    "field": "error_details"
  },
  "timestamp": "2026-05-07T12:34:56Z"
}
```

### Common Error Codes

| Code | Status | Meaning | Example |
|------|--------|---------|---------|
| INVALID_INPUT | 400 | Invalid request data | Missing required field |
| UNAUTHORIZED | 401 | Invalid/missing auth | Invalid API key |
| FORBIDDEN | 403 | Don't have permission | Accessing another user's debt |
| NOT_FOUND | 404 | Resource doesn't exist | Debt ID doesn't exist |
| VALIDATION_ERROR | 422 | Data format wrong | Amount must be number |
| RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED | 429 | Too many requests | Exceeded 1,000/hour |
| SERVER_ERROR | 500 | Our fault | Database error |
| SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE | 503 | Maintenance | Scheduled downtime |

