## Common Use Cases

### Use Case 1: Get All Your Debts

First, authenticate and then list your debts:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  https://api.financialreset.com/v1/debts
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "debts": [
    {
      "debt_id": 1,
      "name": "Chase Credit Card",
      "balance": 2000,
      "interest_rate": 22
    },
    {
      "debt_id": 2,
      "name": "Personal Loan",
      "balance": 5000,
      "interest_rate": 12
    }
  ]
}
```

This shows all debts associated with your account.

---

### Use Case 2: Create and Explore a Hardship Plan

Step 1: See what options are available for a debt:
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  https://api.financialreset.com/v1/hardship/options/1
```

Step 2: Get a recommendation:
```bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "debt_id": 1,
    "monthly_cash_available": 75
  }' \
  https://api.financialreset.com/v1/hardship/recommend
```

Step 3: Calculate the specific option:
```bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "debt_id": 1,
    "reduced_payment": 75,
    "forbearance_months": 6
  }' \
  https://api.financialreset.com/v1/hardship/calculate/forbearance
```

Step 4: Create the plan:
```bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "debt_id": 1,
